    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "private broadcast: Extra guard against unintended non-private broadcast of private transactions",
    "user": {
      "login": "optout21",
      "id": 13562139,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTYyMTM5",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13562139?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/optout21",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Motivation: Reduce the risk of accidental privacy leak happening when broadcasting non-privately a requested transaction that had been previously broadcast privately.\n\nBackground: During the initial phase of private broadcast implementation there were unforeseen instances when a private transaction could get broadcast non-privately (e.g. see #36277 #36330 #36309).\n\nCurrently known pathways:\n\n- Re-submission through `submitpackage`\n- Wallet-rebroadcast (when a private transaction is \"picked up\" by the wallet, and rebrodcast after 1-2 days)\n\nNote that these are being addressed, but other, currently non-identified pathways cannot be excluded.\n\nChange summary: Add a general, extra safeguard: whenever there is a transaction broadcast request, check if the given transaction has been previously broadcast privately, and if so, refuse to broadcast non-privately.\n\nTransaction relay is not affected, as it should not be affected by private broadcast.  When we receive a previously private-broadcast transaction for the first time (it's not yet in our mempool), we relay it as any other relayed transaction. Behavior is unchanged in this regard.\n\nNotes:\n\n- Prerequisite: This is built on top of #36477, as keeping finished private broadcasts in the queue is a prerequisite for this change to work.\n- This proposed change is not an alternative to the use-case specific safeguards, but a complementary one.\n- Testing currently uses the two pathways listed above. When they are closed, testing will be more difficult (i.e., it is hard to establish whether non-private broadcast is prevented by the use-case specific or the present generic guard).\n- The private broadcast queue is not persisted, it doesn't survive node restarts\n- Entries deleted via `abortprivatebroadcast` will be forgotten.\n",
