        }
      ],
      "message": "net_processing: don't announce privately broadcast txs on request\n\nWith -privatebroadcast, sendrawtransaction sends the transaction only\nvia short-lived private broadcast connections and does not add it to\nthe mempool. However, other code paths can later add the same\ntransaction to the mempool and announce it to all peers, which links\nthe transaction to this node:\n- the submitpackage RPC\n- the wallet, on commit and on its periodic resend (e.g. after the\n  transaction came back from the network and was picked up by the\n  wallet)\n- the GUI PSBT broadcast\n- ReattemptInitialBroadcast(), for transactions in the unbroadcast set\n\nAll of these end up in PeerManager::InitiateTxBroadcastToAll(), which\nis also used to relay transactions received from peers. Add a reason\nparameter to it (RELAY or REQUESTED). If the reason is not RELAY and\nthe transaction is known to the private broadcast storage, then do not\nannounce it, remove it from the mempool's unbroadcast set, so that it\nis not retried, and log that.\n\nRelaying a privately broadcast transaction after it was received back\nfrom the network is not affected: at that point the node behaves like\nany other node that received the transaction.\n\nExtend p2p_private_broadcast_then_public.py to check that re-sending\na privately broadcast transaction via submitpackage or via the periodic\nresend of the wallet does not reach a public peer, while another\ntransaction sent the same way does.",
